{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144312-w20-summon-dead-party-member-as-an-ancestor-spirit","id":1144312,"title":"W20. Summon dead party member as an ancestor spirit.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-27T01:54:20-07:00","id":1144312,"title":"W20. Summon dead party member as an ancestor spirit.","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> I am a Storyteller in a crossover chronicle set in a Hong Kong. One of my players has lost his character (Garou) in a fight. He has already generated a new character and played him a little, but suddenly, other players became obsessed with idea of summoning his old character back. One of characters in the group is a theurg, and he's capable of summoning spirits, so I don't know what to say about it. Although, I doubt it is a good idea.<br /> <br /> I'm not certain it is a viable option in RaW, so please enlighten me about it. Is it possible to summon (and bind to a fetish) a deceased Garou as an ancestor spirit?<br /> <br /> And the second question, what besides the game contract can be used to make players to change their mind about such actions? I don't want to say NO or use out-of-game agreements, when I can use in-game matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11161-leeder","name":"Leeder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T04:07:42-07:00","id":1144339,"title":"","content":"Is every werewolf reborn as an ancestor spirit? I think not, to be fair, maybe only the greatest of them. Otherwise Gaia would have a fucking ARMY of garou spirits to unleash on the Wyrm and the battle would have been over a thousand of years ago. And you can't have access to Silent Striders Ancestor spirits, of course.<br /> <br /> So, if you know the name and the proper ritual he sure could try the summon, but the main obstacle I see is for him to be reborn as an ancestor at all. Generally speaking he's probably not even going to be that strong as a fetish, he might offer one of the gifts he knows to the user, tops. Why do you think it's not a good idea anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T05:20:29-07:00","id":1144348,"title":"","content":"The player wouldn't be capable of (and allowed to!) playing two characters at the same time or in a queue. And I don't want to roleplay somebody's character as an NPC as well - it may be offensive. The story of the deceased one is over, it was bright and colourful and fierce, so I see this attempt as some sort of desecrating a memory of a decent child of Gaia.<br /> <br /> So, to the point of capabilities.<br /> <br /> What is this proper ritual? The W20 ritual Summon spirit isn't enough for summoning any kind of spirits? Myself, I treat this ritual as a awfully overpowered ultimative magic, but there are no other means to summon spirits except a bunch of battle gifts. Maybe I should re-phrase: are theurges with the Summon spirit rite able to summon all the spirits and ghosts? And what is required to be reborn as an ancestor spirit? And can werecreatures of different kinds (like Mokole) freely interact with Garou ancestors? I should confess that I can't fully understand all the concepts of spirits in W20, and some of them make me confusing over and over.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11161-leeder","name":"Leeder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T13:53:20-07:00","id":1144531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144312-w20-summon-dead-party-member-as-an-ancestor-spirit?p=1144339#post1144339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is every werewolf reborn as an ancestor spirit? I think not, to be fair, maybe only the greatest of them. Otherwise Gaia would have a fucking ARMY of garou spirits to unleash on the Wyrm and the battle would have been over a thousand of years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind also though that the very nature itself of ancestor spirits is left highly ambiguous, and that they may merely be Umbral reflections of the Garou's personality and memories, rather than the disembodied spirits of actual Garou -- the (Garou) thinking being that if ancestor spirits were actually the souls of departed Garou, then there would be no Garou souls left to reincarnate as Garou (also a central belief among the Garou). There's also a few vague theories floating around that ancestor spirits may actually be ephemera of the Tribal Homelands (although this seems unlikely given that ancestor spirits can exist outside the homelands and do other spirit-stuff).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T17:35:49-07:00","id":1144569,"title":"","content":"The Rite of Summoning should be able to summon Ancestor Spirits. Whether or not they are actually spirits of the dead or some kind of ephemeral construct is undetermined. Usually though they are only contacted through the Ancestors background or in their abodes in their Tribal Homelands. Axis Mundi states that Ancestors will respond to the proper rituals if done in their Umbral home and by members of their tribe. If not done in those circumstances, I would increase both the difficulty and the number of successes needed during the Gnosis roll. The pack might very well encounter their old packmate in a foul mood very offended they are disturbing his rest. If the PC theurge is not of the same tribe and attempts the rite in the Realm, you may just want to rule the spirit appears as hostile (if the rite succeeds) since the proper correspondences were not met. I'd treat any Ancestor spirit as if it was a Jaggling.<br /> <br /> Remember that spirits don't react like ordinary people. They have a nature and purpose, even if it is enigmatic. Ancestor spirits are supposed to be guides for their actual blood descendants of their own tribe, which the other PCs obviously can't be. Contacting him is most likely an intrusion and will offend the spirit, even if it is a packmate.<br /> <br /> Personally, if it happened, I would RP the spirit to be very angry and &quot;betrayed&quot; by how badly his old packmate is treating him.<br /> <br /> Since it sounds like the packmate died when he was young and did not have much renown or power, his spirit is likely not very powerful and could not perform useful tasks.<br /> <br /> Rite of Summoning cannot be used on wraiths or other dead people. That is outside the sphere of the rite.<br /> <br /> From a Garou perspective, I think any pack totem or elders at the sept (if they know about it) would tell your PC that it would not be a good idea. Spirits should not be contacted lightly, and unless they have a very good reason to disturb the rest of their old packmate, it should not be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T20:02:10-07:00","id":1144611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1144312-w20-summon-dead-party-member-as-an-ancestor-spirit?p=1144531#post1144531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind also though that the very nature itself of ancestor spirits is left highly ambiguous, and that they may merely be Umbral reflections of the Garou's personality and memories, rather than the disembodied spirits of actual Garou -- the (Garou) thinking being that if ancestor spirits were actually the souls of departed Garou, then there would be no Garou souls left to reincarnate as Garou (also a central belief among the Garou). There's also a few vague theories floating around that ancestor spirits may actually be ephemera of the Tribal Homelands (although this seems unlikely given that ancestor spirits can exist outside the homelands and do other spirit-stuff).</div> </div> </div> </div>This gets brought up once and isn't really addressed again, much like how the book mentions the possibility that Gaia isn't the sum of everything, but then doesn't really give any other takes the time of day or count of words forever after. It's also more in keeping with Werewolf for spirits to be exactly what they are; other games have the ambiguity territory well-scouted out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 09-27-2017, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T23:19:50-07:00","id":1145986,"title":"","content":"Thank you all!<br /> <br /> The situation was resolved properly thanks to your suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11161-leeder","name":"Leeder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}